cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this audit, its vignette set, or its protocol, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  doomscroll-bias: a paired-vignette audit of gendered and culturally framed
  blame attribution in open-weight LLM judgements of doomscrolling conflict
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered audit asking whether open-weight large language models judge
  relationship conflict involving doomscrolling differently depending on the
  gender of the scrolling partner, and whether that shift differs between North
  American and South Asian cultural framings. The design is a paired
  within-item factorial: 120 authored fictional vignettes, each rendered in six
  conditions (gender male/female/neutral x culture north_american/south_asian)
  so that only names and pronouns differ across the renderings of a given
  vignette, making each vignette its own control. Two open-weight models from
  different labs are queried five times per cell at temperature 0, for 7,200
  calls in total. Alongside the blame-attribution measures the audit reports a
  grounding check: whether the sentence each model returns as its evidence
  actually appears verbatim in the vignette it was shown.
